## 2. AI Program Framework

Every program in WHYspace follows a standard interface:

```typescript
interface AIProgram {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  version: string;
  icon: React.ComponentType;
  component: React.ComponentType<ProgramProps>;

  // Program metadata
  description: string;
  category: ProgramCategory;
  permissions: Permission[];

  // Lifecycle
  onInstall?: () => void;
  onUninstall?: () => void;
  onActivate?: () => void;
  onDeactivate?: () => void;

  // Program-specific system prompt (injected into context)
  systemPrompt?: string;

  // Default window config
  defaultWindow: {
    width: number;
    height: number;
    position?: { x: number; y: number };
    minWidth?: number;
    minHeight?: number;
  };

  // Quick actions for command palette
  commands: Command[];
}
```

### Program Categories

| Category | Programs |
|---|---|
| **Communication** | Core Chat, Voice Nexus |
| **Development** | Code Studio, AI Terminal |
| **Knowledge** | Research Agent, Memory Vault |
| **Creative** | Image Forge, Story Weaver |
| **Automation** | Workflow Automator, Agent Scheduler |
| **System** | Settings, Program Manager, Provider Config |

### Built-in Programs

| Program | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Core Chat** | Conversational AI with full context |
| **Code Studio** | Multi-language code editor + AI pair programmer |
| **Research Agent** | Deep research with source synthesis |
| **Memory Vault** | Visual knowledge graph + memory browser |
| **Image Forge** | AI image generation + editing |
| **Voice Nexus** | Speech-to-text + text-to-speech hub |
| **Workflow Automator** | Visual pipeline builder for AI workflows |
| **AI Terminal** | Shell-like interface for system calls |

