## 3. System Call Architecture

Instead of conventional API calls, programs communicate through a **system call interface** modeled after Unix syscalls.

### Core System Calls

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              SYSTEM CALL LAYER               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  AI Calls                                    │
│    ai.complete(prompt, opts) → Response      │
│    ai.stream(prompt, opts) → Stream<Chunk>   │
│    ai.embed(text) → Vector                   │
│    ai.analyze(image) → Analysis              │
│                                              │
│  Memory Calls                                │
│    memory.store(key, value, meta) → void     │
│    memory.search(query) → Result[]           │
│    memory.delete(id) → void                  │
│    memory.sync() → void                      │
│                                              │
│  Program Calls                               │
│    program.launch(id, params) → PID          │
│    program.kill(pid) → void                  │
│    program.list() → Program[]                │
│    program.pipe(from, to, transform) → void  │
│                                              │
│  File Calls                                  │
│    fs.read(path) → Buffer                    │
│    fs.write(path, data) → void               │
│    fs.list(path) → Entry[]                   │
│    fs.watch(path) → Stream<Event>            │
│                                              │
│  Multimodal Calls                            │
│    vision.analyze(image, prompt) → Analysis   │
│    voice.synthesize(text) → Audio            │
│    voice.transcribe(audio) → Text            │
│    audio.generate(params) → Audio            │
│                                              │
│  Workflow Calls                              │
│    workflow.create(name, steps) → ID         │
│    workflow.execute(id, input) → Output      │
│    workflow.schedule(id, cron) → void        │
│    workflow.status(id) → Status              │
│                                              │
│  System Calls                                │
│    sys.info() → SystemInfo                   │
│    sys.providers() → Provider[]              │
│    sys.config(key) → Value                   │
│    sys.log(level, msg) → void                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Call Flow

```
Program → System Call → Kernel → Provider → AI Model
                              ↓
                         Memory Store
                              ↓
                         Stream Back
```

### Streaming Protocol

All AI system calls are **streaming-first**:

```typescript
// Client receives chunked responses via WebSocket
interface SyscallResponse {
  type: 'chunk' | 'delta' | 'done' | 'error' | 'tool_use';
  id: string;
  data: unknown;
  metadata?: {
    tokens?: number;
    latency?: number;
    provider: string;
    model: string;
  };
}
```

